IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb1-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part V, sections 38 to 45: reducing stated
-- capital (38), adjusting the stated capital account (39), contracts to buy shares (40), commissions (41),
-- dividends (42, 43), and the immunity of shareholders and the lien on shares (45). Section 44 is repealed in
-- this text. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Each rule is named `<what it decides> within s <section>`. Money is a NUMBER of dollars
-- and a name that holds one ends "in dollars". A division that has no meaning (no shares issued) returns
-- NOTHING. The solvency tests of s 38(3) and s 42 read the shared record `Facts for a solvency test in Part V`
-- from cb1-nouns.l4; each reads only the fields it names. The rules on stated capital in this module assume
-- the stated capital provisions apply to the corporation; section 26(11) takes an open-end mutual fund out of
-- them (cb1-part5-shares.l4).

§ `Part V -- Reducing stated capital, adjusting it, dividends (s 38 to s 45)`

§§ `s 38 reducing stated capital`

-- src:601 | 38 (1) Subject to subsection (3), a corporation may by special resolution reduce its stated capital for any purpose including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, for the purpose of
-- src:602 | (a) extinguishing or reducing a liability in respect of an amount unpaid on any share;
-- src:603 | (b) distributing to the holder of an issued share of any class or series of shares an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or series; and
-- src:604 | (c) declaring its stated capital to be reduced by an amount that is not represented by realizable assets.
@ref CBCA s 38(1) other reduction of stated capital (src:601-604)
DECLARE `Purpose of a reduction of stated capital (s 38(1))` IS ONE OF
    `extinguishing or reducing a liability in respect of an amount unpaid on any share`
    `distributing to the holder of an issued share of any class or series of shares an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or series`
    `declaring its stated capital to be reduced by an amount that is not represented by realizable assets`
    `any other purpose`

-- s 38(3): "shall not reduce its stated capital for any purpose other than the purpose mentioned in paragraph
-- (1)(c) if there are reasonable grounds for believing that (a) the corporation is, or would after the
-- reduction be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due; or (b) the realizable value of the
-- corporation's assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities". There is no stated
-- capital term here.
-- src:607 | Limitation
-- src:608 | (3) A corporation shall not reduce its stated capital for any purpose other than the purpose mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) if there are reasonable grounds for believing that
-- src:609 | (a) the corporation is, or would after the reduction be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due; or
-- src:610 | (b) the realizable value of the corporation’s assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities.
@ref CBCA s 38(3) limitation (src:607-610)
GIVEN purpose IS A `Purpose of a reduction of stated capital (s 38(1))`
      facts IS A `Facts for a solvency test in Part V`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is forbidden to reduce its stated capital within s 38(3)` MEANS
        (NOT (purpose EQUALS `declaring its stated capital to be reduced by an amount that is not represented by realizable assets`))
    AND (    facts's `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due`
          OR facts's `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` LESS THAN facts's `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars`)

-- s 38(1): "Subject to subsection (3), a corporation may by special resolution reduce its stated capital".
-- src:601 | 38 (1) Subject to subsection (3), a corporation may by special resolution reduce its stated capital for any purpose including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, for the purpose of
@ref CBCA s 38(1) other reduction of stated capital (src:601)
GIVEN tally IS A `Vote tally`
      `subsection 38(3) forbids the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may reduce its stated capital within s 38(1)` MEANS
        `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally
    AND (NOT `subsection 38(3) forbids the reduction`)

-- src:603 | (b) distributing to the holder of an issued share of any class or series of shares an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or series; and
@ref CBCA s 38(1)(b) other reduction of stated capital (src:603)
GIVEN `the amount distributed to the holder of an issued share, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the distribution is within the limit of s 38(1)(b)` MEANS
    `the amount distributed to the holder of an issued share, in dollars` AT MOST `the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars`

-- src:606 | (2) A special resolution under this section shall specify the stated capital account or accounts from which the reduction of stated capital effected by the special resolution will be deducted.
@ref CBCA s 38(2) contents of special resolution (src:606)
GIVEN `the special resolution specifies the stated capital account or accounts from which the reduction of stated capital will be deducted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the special resolution has the contents s 38(2) requires` MEANS
    `the special resolution specifies the stated capital account or accounts from which the reduction of stated capital will be deducted`

-- src:612 | (4) A creditor of a corporation is entitled to apply to a court for an order compelling a shareholder or other recipient
-- src:613 | (a) to pay to the corporation an amount equal to any liability of the shareholder that was extinguished or reduced contrary to this section; or
-- src:614 | (b) to pay or deliver to the corporation any money or property that was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient as a consequence of a reduction of capital made contrary to this section.
@ref CBCA s 38(4) recovery (src:612-614)
DECLARE `Order a creditor may seek under s 38(4)` IS ONE OF
    `an order compelling a shareholder to pay to the corporation an amount equal to any liability of the shareholder that was extinguished or reduced contrary to section 38`
    `an order compelling a shareholder or other recipient to pay or deliver to the corporation any money or property that was paid or distributed as a consequence of a reduction of capital made contrary to section 38`
    `any other order`

-- src:612 | (4) A creditor of a corporation is entitled to apply to a court for an order compelling a shareholder or other recipient
-- src:613 | (a) to pay to the corporation an amount equal to any liability of the shareholder that was extinguished or reduced contrary to this section; or
-- src:614 | (b) to pay or deliver to the corporation any money or property that was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient as a consequence of a reduction of capital made contrary to this section.
@ref CBCA s 38(4) recovery (src:612-614)
GIVEN order IS AN `Order a creditor may seek under s 38(4)`
      `the applicant is a creditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary-to-section-38 act that the order is about was done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the creditor is entitled to apply to a court for the order within s 38(4)` MEANS
        `the applicant is a creditor of the corporation`
    AND `the contrary-to-section-38 act that the order is about was done`
    AND CONSIDER order
        WHEN `an order compelling a shareholder to pay to the corporation an amount equal to any liability of the shareholder that was extinguished or reduced contrary to section 38` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an order compelling a shareholder or other recipient to pay or deliver to the corporation any money or property that was paid or distributed as a consequence of a reduction of capital made contrary to section 38` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `any other order` THEN FALSE

-- s 38(5): "may not be commenced after two years from the date of the act complained of".
-- src:616 | (5) An action to enforce a liability imposed by this section may not be commenced after two years from the date of the act complained of.
@ref CBCA s 38(5) limitation (src:616)
DECIDE `the two-year limit of s 38(5)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 2
    `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:616 | (5) An action to enforce a liability imposed by this section may not be commenced after two years from the date of the act complained of.
@ref CBCA s 38(5) limitation (src:616)
GIVEN `the date of the act complained of` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to commence an action to enforce a liability imposed by section 38 within s 38(5)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the two-year limit of s 38(5)` `counted from` `the date of the act complained of`

-- src:616 | (5) An action to enforce a liability imposed by this section may not be commenced after two years from the date of the act complained of.
@ref CBCA s 38(5) limitation (src:616)
GIVEN `the date of the act complained of` IS A DATE
      `the day the action was commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the action to enforce a liability imposed by section 38 is in time within s 38(5)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` `the two-year limit of s 38(5)` `the date of the act complained of` `the day the action was commenced`

§§ `s 39 adjustment of the stated capital account`

-- s 39(1): the amount to deduct is the stated capital of the shares of the class or series, multiplied by the
-- number of shares (or fractions) acquired, divided by the number of issued shares of that class or series
-- immediately before. NOTHING where no shares were issued: the division has no meaning.
-- src:619 | 39 (1) On a purchase, redemption or other acquisition by a corporation under section 34, 35, 36, 45 or 190 or paragraph 241(3)(f), of shares or fractions thereof issued by it, the corporation shall deduct from the stated capital account maintained for the class or series of shares of which the shares purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired form a part an amount equal to the result obtained by multiplying the stated capital of the shares of that class or series by the number of shares of that class or series or fractions thereof purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired, divided by the number of issued shares of that class or series immediately before the purchase, redemption or other acquisition.
@ref CBCA s 39(1) adjustment of stated capital account (src:619)
GIVEN `the stated capital of the shares of that class or series, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares or fractions of that class or series purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of issued shares of that class or series immediately before the acquisition` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount to deduct from the stated capital account on an acquisition within s 39(1)` MEANS
    IF `the number of issued shares of that class or series immediately before the acquisition` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the stated capital of the shares of that class or series, in dollars` TIMES `the number of shares or fractions of that class or series purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired` DIVIDED BY `the number of issued shares of that class or series immediately before the acquisition`)

-- src:621 | (2) A corporation shall deduct the amount of a payment made by the corporation to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(g) from the stated capital account maintained for the class or series of shares in respect of which the payment was made.
@ref CBCA s 39(2) idem (src:621)
GIVEN `the balance of the stated capital account for the class or series, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the payment made to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(g), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the balance of the stated capital account after the payment within s 39(2)` MEANS
    `the balance of the stated capital account for the class or series, in dollars` MINUS `the amount of the payment made to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(g), in dollars`

-- src:623 | (3) A corporation shall adjust its stated capital account or accounts in accordance with any special resolution referred to in subsection 38(2).
@ref CBCA s 39(3) idem (src:623)
GIVEN `a special resolution referred to in subsection 38(2) has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must adjust its stated capital accounts in accordance with the special resolution within s 39(3)` MEANS
    `a special resolution referred to in subsection 38(2) has been passed`

-- s 39(4): on a conversion or a change of issued shares into another class or series, deduct from the old
-- account the same proportion (paragraph (a)) and add it, with any additional consideration, to the new
-- account (paragraph (b)).
-- src:625 | (4) On a conversion of issued shares of a corporation into shares of another class or series or a change under section 173, 191 or 241 of issued shares of a corporation into shares of another class or series, the corporation shall
-- src:626 | (a) deduct from the stated capital account maintained for the class or series of shares converted or changed an amount equal to the result obtained by multiplying the stated capital of the shares of that class or series by the number of shares of that class or series converted or changed, divided by the number of issued shares of that class or series immediately before the conversion or change; and
@ref CBCA s 39(4)(a) idem (src:625-626)
GIVEN `the stated capital of the shares of the class or series converted or changed, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares of that class or series converted or changed` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of issued shares of that class or series immediately before the conversion or change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount to deduct on a conversion or change within s 39(4)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the number of issued shares of that class or series immediately before the conversion or change` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the stated capital of the shares of the class or series converted or changed, in dollars` TIMES `the number of shares of that class or series converted or changed` DIVIDED BY `the number of issued shares of that class or series immediately before the conversion or change`)

-- src:625 | (4) On a conversion of issued shares of a corporation into shares of another class or series or a change under section 173, 191 or 241 of issued shares of a corporation into shares of another class or series, the corporation shall
-- src:627 | (b) add the result obtained under paragraph (a) and any additional consideration received pursuant to the conversion or change to the stated capital account maintained or to be maintained for the class or series of shares into which the shares have been converted or changed.
@ref CBCA s 39(4)(b) idem (src:625 src:627)
GIVEN `the amount deducted under paragraph 39(4)(a), in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the additional consideration received pursuant to the conversion or change, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount to add on a conversion or change within s 39(4)(b)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount deducted under paragraph 39(4)(a), in dollars`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST deducted THEN JUST (deducted PLUS `the additional consideration received pursuant to the conversion or change, in dollars`)

-- s 39(5): where the corporation issues two classes with a right to convert each into the other, the stated
-- capital attributable to a share in either class, on a conversion, is the aggregate of the stated capital of
-- both classes divided by the number of issued shares of both classes immediately before. "Subject to its
-- articles": NOTHING where the articles provide otherwise. Section 26(5) refers to "two classes of convertible
-- shares referred to in subsection 39(5)": that is the first rule below.
-- src:629 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4) and subject to its articles, where a corporation issues two classes of shares and there is attached to each such class a right to convert a share of the one class into a share of the other class, if a share of one class is converted into a share of the other class, the amount of stated capital attributable to a share in either class is the aggregate of the stated capital of both classes divided by the number of issued shares of both classes immediately before the conversion.
@ref CBCA s 39(5) stated capital of interconvertible shares (src:629)
GIVEN `the corporation issues two classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is attached to each class a right to convert a share of the one class into a share of the other` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has two classes of convertible shares referred to in s 39(5)` MEANS
        `the corporation issues two classes of shares`
    AND `there is attached to each class a right to convert a share of the one class into a share of the other`

-- src:629 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4) and subject to its articles, where a corporation issues two classes of shares and there is attached to each such class a right to convert a share of the one class into a share of the other class, if a share of one class is converted into a share of the other class, the amount of stated capital attributable to a share in either class is the aggregate of the stated capital of both classes divided by the number of issued shares of both classes immediately before the conversion.
@ref CBCA s 39(5) stated capital of interconvertible shares (src:629)
GIVEN `the articles provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stated capital of the first class, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the stated capital of the second class, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of issued shares of the first class immediately before the conversion` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of issued shares of the second class immediately before the conversion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the stated capital attributable to a share in either class within s 39(5)` MEANS
    IF `the articles provide otherwise` OR (`the number of issued shares of the first class immediately before the conversion` PLUS `the number of issued shares of the second class immediately before the conversion` EQUALS 0)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((`the stated capital of the first class, in dollars` PLUS `the stated capital of the second class, in dollars`) DIVIDED BY (`the number of issued shares of the first class immediately before the conversion` PLUS `the number of issued shares of the second class immediately before the conversion`))

-- src:631 | (6) Shares or fractions thereof of any class or series of shares issued by a corporation and purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired by it shall be cancelled or, if the articles limit the number of authorized shares, may be restored to the status of authorized but unissued shares of the class.
@ref CBCA s 39(6) cancellation or restoration of shares (src:631)
DECLARE `What becomes of shares a corporation has acquired (s 39(6))` IS ONE OF
    `the shares must be cancelled`
    `the shares must be cancelled or may be restored to the status of authorized but unissued shares of the class`

-- src:631 | (6) Shares or fractions thereof of any class or series of shares issued by a corporation and purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired by it shall be cancelled or, if the articles limit the number of authorized shares, may be restored to the status of authorized but unissued shares of the class.
@ref CBCA s 39(6) cancellation or restoration of shares (src:631)
GIVEN `the articles limit the number of authorized shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What becomes of shares a corporation has acquired (s 39(6))`
`what becomes of the acquired shares within s 39(6)` MEANS
    IF `the articles limit the number of authorized shares`
    THEN `the shares must be cancelled or may be restored to the status of authorized but unissued shares of the class`
    ELSE `the shares must be cancelled`

-- src:633 | (7) For the purposes of this section, a corporation holding shares in itself as permitted by subsections 31(1) and (2) is deemed not to have purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired such shares.
@ref CBCA s 39(7) exception (src:633)
GIVEN `the corporation holds the shares in itself as permitted by subsection 31(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is deemed not to have purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired the shares for the purposes of s 39 within s 39(7)` MEANS
    `the corporation holds the shares in itself as permitted by subsection 31(1) or (2)`

-- s 39(8): shares held as permitted by paragraph 32(1)(a), and shares into which they were converted and held
-- under paragraph 32(1)(b), that the corporation still holds at the expiration of two years are deemed to have
-- been acquired at the expiration of the two years (counted from the day the shares, or the shares from which
-- they were converted, were acquired). NOTHING: the shares are not held then, so there is no deemed
-- acquisition; or they are not shares to which the subsection applies.
-- src:635 | (8) For the purposes of this section, a corporation holding shares in itself as permitted by paragraph 32(1)(a) is deemed not to have purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired the shares at the time they were acquired, but
-- src:636 | (a) any of those shares that are held by the corporation at the expiration of two years, and
-- src:637 | (b) any shares into which any of those shares were converted by the corporation and held under paragraph 32(1)(b) that are held by the corporation at the expiration of two years after the shares from which they were converted were acquired
-- src:638 | are deemed to have been acquired at the expiration of the two years.
@ref CBCA s 39(8) idem (src:635-638)
DECIDE `the two-year limit of s 39(8)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 2
    `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:635 | (8) For the purposes of this section, a corporation holding shares in itself as permitted by paragraph 32(1)(a) is deemed not to have purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired the shares at the time they were acquired, but
-- src:636 | (a) any of those shares that are held by the corporation at the expiration of two years, and
-- src:637 | (b) any shares into which any of those shares were converted by the corporation and held under paragraph 32(1)(b) that are held by the corporation at the expiration of two years after the shares from which they were converted were acquired
-- src:638 | are deemed to have been acquired at the expiration of the two years.
@ref CBCA s 39(8) idem (src:635-638)
GIVEN `the shares are held as permitted by paragraph 32(1)(a), or are shares into which such shares were converted and are held under paragraph 32(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the shares, or the shares from which they were converted, were acquired` IS A DATE
      `the corporation holds the shares at the expiration of the two years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the shares are deemed to have been acquired within s 39(8)` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held as permitted by paragraph 32(1)(a), or are shares into which such shares were converted and are held under paragraph 32(1)(b)` AND `the corporation holds the shares at the expiration of the two years`
    THEN JUST (`the last day of` `the two-year limit of s 39(8)` `counted from` `the day the shares, or the shares from which they were converted, were acquired`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:640 | (9) Shares issued by a corporation and converted into shares of another class or series or changed under section 173, 191 or 241 into shares of another class or series shall become issued shares of the class or series of shares into which the shares have been converted or changed.
@ref CBCA s 39(9) conversion or change of shares (src:640)
GIVEN `the shares were issued by the corporation and converted into shares of another class or series, or changed under section 173, 191 or 241 into shares of another class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shares become issued shares of the class or series into which they were converted or changed within s 39(9)` MEANS
    `the shares were issued by the corporation and converted into shares of another class or series, or changed under section 173, 191 or 241 into shares of another class or series`

-- s 39(10): where the articles limit the authorized shares of a class and issued shares of it have become
-- issued shares of another class by subsection (9), the unissued shares of the first class are increased by
-- that number, "unless the articles otherwise provide". NOTHING where the articles do not limit the number.
-- src:642 | (10) Where the articles limit the number of authorized shares of a class of shares of a corporation and issued shares of that class or of a series of shares of that class have become, pursuant to subsection (9), issued shares of another class or series, the number of unissued shares of the first-mentioned class shall, unless the articles otherwise provide, be increased by the number of shares that, pursuant to subsection (9), became shares of another class or series.
@ref CBCA s 39(10) effect of change of shares on number of unissued shares (src:642)
GIVEN `the articles limit the number of authorized shares of the first class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of unissued shares of the first class before the change` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares that became shares of another class or series` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of unissued shares of the first class after the change within s 39(10)` MEANS
    IF `the articles limit the number of authorized shares of the first class`
    THEN IF `the articles otherwise provide`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (`the number of unissued shares of the first class before the change` PLUS `the number of shares that became shares of another class or series`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:644 | (11) Debt obligations issued, pledged, hypothecated or deposited by a corporation are not redeemed by reason only that the indebtedness evidenced by the debt obligations or in respect of which the debt obligations are issued, pledged, hypothecated or deposited is repaid.
@ref CBCA s 39(11) repayment (src:644)
GIVEN `the indebtedness is repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt obligations are redeemed on a ground other than that the indebtedness is repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the debt obligations are redeemed within s 39(11)` MEANS
    `the debt obligations are redeemed on a ground other than that the indebtedness is repaid`

-- src:646 | (12) Debt obligations issued by a corporation and purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired by it may be cancelled or, subject to any applicable trust indenture or other agreement, may be reissued, pledged or hypothecated to secure any obligation of the corporation then existing or thereafter incurred, and any such acquisition and reissue, pledge or hypothecation is not a cancellation of the debt obligations.
@ref CBCA s 39(12) acquisition and reissue of debt obligations (src:646)
GIVEN `an applicable trust indenture or other agreement prohibits the reissue, pledge or hypothecation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may reissue, pledge or hypothecate the acquired debt obligations within s 39(12)` MEANS
    NOT `an applicable trust indenture or other agreement prohibits the reissue, pledge or hypothecation`

-- src:646 | (12) Debt obligations issued by a corporation and purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired by it may be cancelled or, subject to any applicable trust indenture or other agreement, may be reissued, pledged or hypothecated to secure any obligation of the corporation then existing or thereafter incurred, and any such acquisition and reissue, pledge or hypothecation is not a cancellation of the debt obligations.
@ref CBCA s 39(12) acquisition and reissue of debt obligations (src:646)
GIVEN `the debt obligations were acquired by the corporation and then reissued, pledged or hypothecated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the acquisition and reissue, pledge or hypothecation is a cancellation of the debt obligations within s 39(12)` MEANS
    FALSE

§§ `s 40 and s 41 contracts to buy shares; commission`

-- src:648 | 40 (1) A corporation shall fulfil its obligations under a contract to buy shares of the corporation, except if the corporation can prove that enforcement of the contract would put it in breach of any of sections 34 to 36.
@ref CBCA s 40(1) enforcement of contract to buy shares (src:648)
GIVEN `the corporation can prove that enforcement of the contract would put it in breach of section 34, 35 or 36` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must fulfil its obligations under the contract to buy shares within s 40(1)` MEANS
    NOT `the corporation can prove that enforcement of the contract would put it in breach of section 34, 35 or 36`

-- s 40(2): until the corporation has fulfilled all its obligations, the other party "retains the status of
-- claimant entitled to be paid as soon as the corporation is lawfully able to do so or, in a liquidation, to be
-- ranked subordinate to the rights of creditors and to the rights of holders of any class of shares whose
-- rights were in priority to the rights given to the holders of the class of shares being purchased, but in
-- priority to the rights of other shareholders".
-- src:650 | (2) Until the corporation has fulfilled all its obligations under a contract referred to in subsection (1), the other party retains the status of claimant entitled to be paid as soon as the corporation is lawfully able to do so or, in a liquidation, to be ranked subordinate to the rights of creditors and to the rights of holders of any class of shares whose rights were in priority to the rights given to the holders of the class of shares being purchased, but in priority to the rights of other shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 40(2) status of contracting party (src:650)
DECLARE `Person ranked against the claimant in a liquidation (s 40(2))` IS ONE OF
    `a creditor of the corporation`
    `a holder of a class of shares whose rights were in priority to the rights given to the holders of the class of shares being purchased`
    `a holder of any other shares`
    `any other person`

-- src:650 | (2) Until the corporation has fulfilled all its obligations under a contract referred to in subsection (1), the other party retains the status of claimant entitled to be paid as soon as the corporation is lawfully able to do so or, in a liquidation, to be ranked subordinate to the rights of creditors and to the rights of holders of any class of shares whose rights were in priority to the rights given to the holders of the class of shares being purchased, but in priority to the rights of other shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 40(2) status of contracting party (src:650)
GIVEN person IS A `Person ranked against the claimant in a liquidation (s 40(2))`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the claimant ranks in priority to the person in a liquidation within s 40(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `a creditor of the corporation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a holder of a class of shares whose rights were in priority to the rights given to the holders of the class of shares being purchased` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a holder of any other shares` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other person` THEN NOTHING

-- src:650 | (2) Until the corporation has fulfilled all its obligations under a contract referred to in subsection (1), the other party retains the status of claimant entitled to be paid as soon as the corporation is lawfully able to do so or, in a liquidation, to be ranked subordinate to the rights of creditors and to the rights of holders of any class of shares whose rights were in priority to the rights given to the holders of the class of shares being purchased, but in priority to the rights of other shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 40(2) status of contracting party (src:650)
GIVEN `the corporation has fulfilled all its obligations under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is lawfully able to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the other party is entitled to be paid within s 40(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation has fulfilled all its obligations under the contract`)
    AND `the corporation is lawfully able to pay`

-- src:652 | 41 The directors may authorize the corporation to pay a reasonable commission to any person in consideration of the person’s purchasing or agreeing to purchase shares of the corporation from the corporation or from any other person, or procuring or agreeing to procure purchasers for any such shares.
@ref CBCA s 41 commission for sale of shares (src:652)
GIVEN `the commission is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in consideration of the person's purchasing or agreeing to purchase shares of the corporation from the corporation or from any other person, or procuring or agreeing to procure purchasers for such shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may authorize the corporation to pay the commission within s 41` MEANS
        `the commission is reasonable`
    AND `it is in consideration of the person's purchasing or agreeing to purchase shares of the corporation from the corporation or from any other person, or procuring or agreeing to procure purchasers for such shares`

§§ `s 42 and s 43 dividends`

-- s 42: "shall not declare or pay a dividend if there are reasonable grounds for believing that (a) ... unable
-- to pay its liabilities as they become due; or (b) the realizable value of the corporation's assets would
-- thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities and stated capital of all classes". For an open-end
-- mutual fund the stated capital provisions do not apply (s 26(11)), so its stated capital term is nil (fork
-- cb1-F9 in NOTES.md).
-- src:654 | 42 A corporation shall not declare or pay a dividend if there are reasonable grounds for believing that
-- src:655 | (a) the corporation is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due; or
-- src:656 | (b) the realizable value of the corporation’s assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities and stated capital of all classes.
@ref CBCA s 42 dividends (src:654-656)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for a solvency test in Part V`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is forbidden to declare or pay a dividend within s 42` MEANS
        facts's `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due`
    OR  facts's `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` LESS THAN (facts's `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars`) PLUS (IF facts's `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund` THEN 0 ELSE facts's `stated capital of all classes, in dollars`)

-- s 43(1): "may pay a dividend by issuing fully paid shares of the corporation and, subject to section 42, ... in
-- money or property". Section 42 forbids "a dividend" without limit; it is read to reach a share dividend as
-- well (fork cb1-F10 in NOTES.md).
-- src:658 | 43 (1) A corporation may pay a dividend by issuing fully paid shares of the corporation and, subject to section 42, a corporation may pay a dividend in money or property.
@ref CBCA s 43(1) form of dividend (src:658)
DECLARE `Form of a dividend (s 43(1))` IS ONE OF
    `by issuing fully paid shares of the corporation`
    `in money`
    `in property`
    `any other form`

-- src:658 | 43 (1) A corporation may pay a dividend by issuing fully paid shares of the corporation and, subject to section 42, a corporation may pay a dividend in money or property.
@ref CBCA s 43(1) form of dividend (src:658)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of a dividend (s 43(1))`
      `section 42 forbids the dividend` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may pay the dividend in that form within s 43(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `section 42 forbids the dividend`)
    AND CONSIDER form
        WHEN `by issuing fully paid shares of the corporation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `in money` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `in property` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `any other form` THEN FALSE

-- src:660 | (2) If shares of a corporation are issued in payment of a dividend, the declared amount of the dividend stated as an amount of money shall be added to the stated capital account maintained or to be maintained for the shares of the class or series issued in payment of the dividend.
@ref CBCA s 43(2) adjustment of stated capital account (src:660)
GIVEN `shares of the corporation are issued in payment of a dividend` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declared amount of the dividend stated as an amount of money, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount to add to the stated capital account for the class or series issued within s 43(2)` MEANS
    IF `shares of the corporation are issued in payment of a dividend`
    THEN JUST `the declared amount of the dividend stated as an amount of money, in dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 45 shareholder immunity; lien or hypothec`

-- s 45(1): the shareholders "are not, as shareholders, liable for any liability, act or default of the
-- corporation except under subsection 38(4), 118(4) or (5), 146(5) or 226(4) or (5)".
-- src:663 | 45 (1) The shareholders of a corporation are not, as shareholders, liable for any liability, act or default of the corporation except under subsection 38(4), 118(4) or (5), 146(5) or 226(4) or (5).
@ref CBCA s 45(1) shareholder immunity (src:663)
DECLARE `Basis on which a shareholder is said to be liable for the corporation's liability, act or default (s 45(1))` IS ONE OF
    `as a shareholder only`
    `under subsection 38(4)`
    `under subsection 118(4) or (5)`
    `under subsection 146(5)`
    `under subsection 226(4) or (5)`

-- src:663 | 45 (1) The shareholders of a corporation are not, as shareholders, liable for any liability, act or default of the corporation except under subsection 38(4), 118(4) or (5), 146(5) or 226(4) or (5).
@ref CBCA s 45(1) shareholder immunity (src:663)
GIVEN basis IS A `Basis on which a shareholder is said to be liable for the corporation's liability, act or default (s 45(1))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 45(1) shields the shareholder from the liability within s 45(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `as a shareholder only` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `under subsection 38(4)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `under subsection 118(4) or (5)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `under subsection 146(5)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `under subsection 226(4) or (5)` THEN FALSE

-- s 45(2): "Subject to subsection 49(8), the articles may provide that the corporation has a lien or hypothec on a
-- share registered in the name of a shareholder or the shareholder's personal representative for a debt of
-- that shareholder to the corporation, including an amount unpaid in respect of a share issued by a body
-- corporate on the date it was continued under this Act."
-- src:665 | (2) Subject to subsection 49(8), the articles may provide that the corporation has a lien or hypothec on a share registered in the name of a shareholder or the shareholder’s personal representative for a debt of that shareholder to the corporation, including an amount unpaid in respect of a share issued by a body corporate on the date it was continued under this Act.
@ref CBCA s 45(2) lien or hypothec on shares (src:665)
GIVEN `the share is registered in the name of a shareholder or the shareholder's personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lien or hypothec is for a debt of that shareholder to the corporation, including an amount unpaid in respect of a share issued by a body corporate on the date it was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 49(8) forbids it` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 49(8) (piece cb2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles may provide that the corporation has a lien or hypothec on the share within s 45(2)` MEANS
        `the share is registered in the name of a shareholder or the shareholder's personal representative`
    AND `the lien or hypothec is for a debt of that shareholder to the corporation, including an amount unpaid in respect of a share issued by a body corporate on the date it was continued under this Act`
    AND (NOT `subsection 49(8) forbids it`)

-- src:667 | (3) A corporation may enforce a lien or hypothec referred to in subsection (2) in accordance with its by-laws.
@ref CBCA s 45(3) enforcement of lien or hypothec (src:667)
GIVEN `a lien or hypothec referred to in subsection 45(2) exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enforcement is in accordance with the by-laws of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may enforce the lien or hypothec within s 45(3)` MEANS
        `a lien or hypothec referred to in subsection 45(2) exists`
    AND `the enforcement is in accordance with the by-laws of the corporation`
